{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And you shall find.</b> It would have been fitting to say ומצאתם — in the plural. But had it said so, it would appear that only the many who seek HaShem from within their exile will find Him when they seek Him, but not so the individual, for the merit of the many is great, as they said: 'the Holy One, blessed be He, does not despise the prayer of the many,' as it is said (Job 36:5): ״הן אל כביר ולא ימאס״. Therefore it says ומצאת — in the singular — to teach you that even the individual finds Him when he seeks Him with all his heart and with all his soul, and his case will not be subsumed under the many, to be counted merely within their number."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:29.218700031Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}